and has intricate designs carved into it. He ¹ “diagramist” and this 
¹ device he uses to diagram the musician’s compositions. He him- 
self is very talented. He has several “fonts” ± sheets of music that 
emerge from his device are beautifully proportioned and visually per- 
fect. I understand ē work ¢ diagramist allows the composer 
the freedom to be the wild, almost ethereal talent â, because the 
diagramist will capture the music on paper and make of it another form 
of art, allowing it to endure. 
